{"kind":"request","text":"C2 next step after the complete adopted recovery design eea6271d and satisfied originalcf9050b4: prepare the separately reviewable concrete stage-one execution commission. Design/preparation only; do not run or deploy the probe yet. Amend the existing dated recovery note/corrections/map rather than invent a second architecture or shrink the original scope.\n\nFirst read and declare the relevant actual adopted R1v11, R2v14 and R4v9 inputs, reconcile their status and the nonblocking late-output suffix wording recorded in d268cae0: receipted commands can append late output; the interruption rule is for unreceipted attempts. Coordinate common identities/receipt seams with existing d56d7f65. Keep the provider assumptions and stage-two dependencies explicitly unproved wherever that is their actual state.\n\nMake stage one request-ready: select and identify exact provider, SDK/runtime/image versions and controller store/storage APIs using primary documented evidence; name the trusted boundary and proposed command for the real owned storage/process probe. State transaction and conditional-write semantics, actual host interruption/termination mechanism, containment and writer-freeze/census mechanism, immutable payload upload/readback/hash closure, manifest and receipt job-cut join, exact Git/object restoration, durable journal ownership and deletion generation/tombstone handling. Dispose the stage-one-critical RU choices, or explicitly state the concrete missing prerequisite that prevents execution. Optional stage-two questions must not silently become stage-one prerequisites.\n\nName bounded test resources, storage sizes, runtime/timeouts, maximum spend, credentials/custody, output/redaction paths and cleanup ownership. Give an operation ledger for setup, writes, interruption, restore and deletion, including uncertain outcomes that must remain held rather than be blindly retried or declared cleaned. Named disposable owned objects may be removed when settled; identifying or retaining an unknown duty is a result, not a cleanup failure to conceal. Do not touch production or earlier spike resources. No unbounded provider exploration or unrelated external resource inventory.\n\nKeep the nine compact real-boundary cases from the adopted design: abrupt host loss; detached writer; stale instance/epoch/prior plus duplicate callback; failed save in both surviving-instance and prior-root-restoration orders; missing/corrupt saved data; exact unpushed commit; interrupted nonreplayable side effect; a distinct authorized second attempt preserving the earlier unknown duty; and pins/expiry/deletion retry/lost reply/tombstone. Name the actual outcome artifact, oracle, version, elapsed-time and cost record for each. Reuse one meaningful shared scenario/fixture where lawful; avoid field sweeps, sleeps and duplicate whole-product gates. Stage one proves real storage/process boundaries only, with trusted supervisor claims labelled. The full stage-two owner/admin/device/hold/fork/token/custody/takeover/export/proposal/review/publication outcome remains owed under the same68-row map, with actual adopted/reviewed interfaces before integrated proof.\n\nDeliver complete exact-head artifacts and ordinary independent review before planner considers the concrete execution commission. This preparation does not authorize source scripts, installs, tests, typechecks, private diagnostics, provider probes, deployment or credential changes. Highest-priority10x useful-test economy, current I1 review and builder judgment of Jam entry remain; this is no new first-Jam checklist.","body":{"conditions":"Prepare a concrete, reviewable stage-one commission in the existing C2 design package, reconciled with adopted interfaces. Name actual provider/SDK/version, command, resources/cost, storage/process/transaction boundaries, bounded owned cleanup and meaningful nine-case evidence. Ordinary independent review and explicit later commission precede execution